# BloodConnect BD Project Guardrails

Before implementation, read `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, and `docs/01_PRD.md` through `docs/06_Plan.md`. Read supporting docs relevant to the task.

- Use `docs/06_Plan.md` as the task queue. Respect dependencies.
- After every completed step, update `docs/06_Plan.md` with status, files, commands, actual results and remaining work.
- Do not mark a task VERIFIED without reproducible test evidence.
- Use a modular Django monolith, PostgreSQL, Django templates + Bootstrap, and DRF `/api/v1/`.
- Django ORM is the only application database access path. Never expose PostgreSQL directly to clients.
- Donor contact information and precise location remain private until an explicit donor acceptance workflow permits disclosure.
- The platform only discovers potential donors and coordinates contact. It never determines medical eligibility or transfusion compatibility and never collects, tests, stores, sells or transfuses blood.
- Government, hospital and blood-bank integrations require documented authorization and credentials. Use mock adapters otherwise.
- Never hardcode secrets or use real personal/health data in fixtures or logs.
- Enforce server-side authorization, CSRF, input validation, rate limits and safe upload handling.
- Document architecture changes in `docs/12_Architecture_ADRs.md` before implementing them.
